This folder is one student's binder. Everything you do in this session is
about this student and no one else.

Before doing anything else, read this student's four files:

1. `<StudentName>.md` — interests, current lesson topics, Concept sequence
   (most recent last), recent errors, notes
2. `sounds.md` — the sound/concept catalog and which rows are marked known
3. `sight-words.md` — the sight-word list and which words are marked known
4. `lesson-plans/` — the last 3 lesson plans, by date in the filename

The `Known` flags in sounds.md and sight-words.md are the only authority on
what this student can read. Never infer what they know from a row's position,
their grade, or what they "should" know by now.

Then follow the instructions in `../../_guide/`:

- `_guide/onboarding.md` — setting this student up, or transcribing a paper
  checklist into the Known flags.
- `_guide/lesson-planning.md` — writing a lesson plan. Read it every time;
  do not write a plan from memory.

Save each lesson plan to `lesson-plans/YYYY-MM-DD-concept.md`, built from
`../../lesson-plan-template.md`. Update the student's profile as they learn:
add to the Concept sequence, and record new errors with the WHY, not just the
word.
